#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# is_dataset

#% text
# `is_dataset(x)` gives `true` if `x` is a dataset, and `false` otherwise.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# A dataset is the term `dataset(assoc(c1 -> col1, ...))` with columns of one length, as `dataset` makes it.

#% item
# An association of columns is not a dataset until `dataset` is applied to it.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# A dataset and an association:

#% cell
is_dataset(dataset(assoc("a" -> [1, 2])))
#% output
#= true

#% cell
is_dataset(assoc("a" -> [1, 2]))
#% output
#= false

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# Selecting the datasets of a list:

#% cell
select([dataset([]), [], 3, dataset(assoc("x" -> [0]))], is_dataset)
#% output
#= [dataset(assoc()), dataset(assoc("x" -> [0]))]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `dataset`, `is_assoc`
